# The test songs are sound, never text: a Windows checkout must not touch their line endings (git already
# takes them for binary, since they hold zero bytes; this says so for good, and for any test file added later).
# The text files here (the checks, the README) keep plain line endings on every computer. Order matters: the
# general line first, the binary ones after it, so they win.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.mp3 binary
*.m4a binary
*.wav binary
*.aiff binary
*.aif binary
*.flac binary
*.aac binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
